# Allowed differences from the golden prompt copies for spec
# 006-specforge-kritis-profile — a DOCUMENTED exception to FR-008/SC-002:
# two additions are allowed in SKILL.md, none elsewhere (plan Commit 2+/Wave 8):
# (1) the German alias "erstelle eine Spezifikation"
# added to the a1-new-feature description (wave-plan Wave 1 brief item 3); (2) review fix M1 (2026-10-30): one
# unguarded "Profile resolve" line, with its blank separator, after the Roadmap
# Gate. FR-001 auto-enable needs resolve to run on a run WITHOUT --profile, so it
# cannot sit inside a block whose guard says "skip unless the run profile is
# kritis". The line only reads (profile resolve writes nothing) and prints
# profile:null for a project that never declared one.
# Every OTHER line of every prompt file must be byte-identical once the
# `<!-- a1-profile:kritis -->` ... `<!-- /a1-profile:kritis -->` blocks are
# stripped (fixtures/strip-blocks.cjs) — this file carries no allowance for
# anything inside those blocks; blocks are compared by their own mechanism
# (strip, then cmp), not by this allowed-diff.
#
# Format: <file><TAB><ext><TAB><op><TAB><text>
#   insert-after: the golden line <text> must occur exactly once in the
#   named file; the following "line" rules are inserted after it, so the
#   current file must carry exactly those lines there. Applied with
#   golden/apply-prompts-allowed.cjs, which exits 3 when an allowance
#   matches zero or two lines — an allowance that no longer matches cannot
#   pass silently.
#
# Anchor note: this anchors on the existing alias-list line of SKILL.md's
# `description:` block (a YAML folded scalar — each physical line below is
# literal text, not a logical sentence). Wave 8 owns the exact wording; if
# it inserts the alias at a different point in the description, or phrases
# it differently, THIS FILE must be updated in the same commit as that
# prompt edit (the wiring wave's own acceptance: "the only edit outside a
# block is the allowed description alias", checked by parts/08-wiring.sh's
# `git diff "$GOLDEN_COMMIT"...HEAD` on the six prompt files).
SKILL.md	md	insert-after	  <projekt>"), "spec for <project>" (alias: "spec für <projekt>"), "feature pipeline",
SKILL.md	md	line	  "a1-new-feature", "erstelle eine Spezifikation" (German alias for "spec for <project>"),
SKILL.md	md	insert-after	`a1-roadmap`'s SKILL.md.
SKILL.md	md	line	
SKILL.md	md	line	**Profile resolve (every run, before Phase 1).** Run `node <repo>/_shared/a1-tools.cjs profile resolve [--profile <name>] --repo-root <repo> [--spec <path>]`; exit 1 or 2 stops the run. When the printed `profile` is `kritis`, the blocks marked `a1-profile:kritis` apply to this run; otherwise ignore them.
#
# Spec 024-ux-studio (a1-ux-studio, Wave 7) — pure insertions, no golden line touched:
# (1) SKILL.md: `  - Skill` in allowed-tools (FR-015: the main session invokes the studio via the Skill tool).
# (2) SKILL.md: one vf-brand row in "Design-System Skill per Project" (design-system routing for Vodafone projects).
# (3) 03-clarify.md: sub-step 2b-2a "Rendered options via a1-ux-studio (size M/L)" between 2b-2 and 2b-3 (FR-015).
# None of it sits inside an a1-profile:kritis block. Anchors are golden lines that occur exactly once.
SKILL.md	md	insert-after	  - Agent
SKILL.md	md	line	  - Skill
SKILL.md	md	insert-after	same id used for `code-scope stage`/`release` in the Completion Gate below.
SKILL.md	md	line	Single definition (it supersedes the example): `workflows/00-roadmap-gate.md`, section `<spec-id>`.
SKILL.md	md	insert-after	| Projects using n3ural design system | `n3urala1-design` (`~/.claude/skills/n3urala1-design`) |
SKILL.md	md	line	| Projects using the Vodafone brand design system | `vf-brand` (`~/.claude/skills/vf-brand`) |
03-clarify.md	md	insert-after	> - Phase 3 ends only when ALL markers are gone (0 remaining).
03-clarify.md	md	line	> - If `AskUserQuestion` is unavailable in this run: return a numbered question queue and stop; the orchestrator asks and
03-clarify.md	md	line	>   resumes you (`01-discover.md` Step 3, question relay).
03-clarify.md	md	insert-after	Fallback if no design system is specified: `frontend-design`.
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	### 2b-2a — Rendered options via a1-ux-studio (size M/L)
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	Read `size:` from the spec frontmatter. A missing or unclear value counts as M
03-clarify.md	md	line	(the size triage rule "any doubt → M").
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	| `size:` | What happens |
03-clarify.md	md	line	|---|---|
03-clarify.md	md	line	| M or L | Run the studio for every screen from 2b-1 (this sub-step). |
03-clarify.md	md	line	| S | Size S only on request: skip this sub-step and go to 2b-3 (ASCII wireframes), unless the user asks for rendered variants. Then run it like M. |
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	For each screen from 2b-1, the main session (this orchestrator) uses the
03-clarify.md	md	line	Skill tool to invoke `a1-specforge:a1-ux-studio`. Pass the spec id, the project
03-clarify.md	md	line	slug, the screen name, the design-system skill from 2b-2 and the relevant FRs.
03-clarify.md	md	line	The studio runs in this session with the user, one run folder per screen.
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	After the studio's step 6 (handoff check exit 0), the main session appends to
03-clarify.md	md	line	`## Clarifications` in `<spec-path>`, one entry per screen:
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	```
03-clarify.md	md	line	- **YYYY-MM-DD** — UX/<screen-name>: Variant <X> chosen. Reason: <1-sentence>.
03-clarify.md	md	line	  Run: <link to the run folder's run.md>
03-clarify.md	md	line	```
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	Write no entry for a screen whose handoff stays blocked; ask the user how to proceed.
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	**Effect on 2b-3:** when 2b-2a ran for a screen, Uwe receives the chosen
03-clarify.md	md	line	direction (the entry above and the run link) and writes the UX Decision instead
03-clarify.md	md	line	of drawing ASCII variants: he confirms the entry matches the chosen variant and
03-clarify.md	md	line	adds his handoff notes beneath it, without a second `UX/` line. Screens the
03-clarify.md	md	line	studio did not cover go through 2b-3 unchanged.
03-clarify.md	md	line	
03-clarify.md	md	line	**Fallback:** if the studio is unavailable (skill not installed, or it stops
03-clarify.md	md	line	because `A1_VAULT_ROOT` is unset), tell the user why and run 2b-3 with ASCII
03-clarify.md	md	line	wireframes as before.
